&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Learning Operations &amp;amp; Transformation Manager is an enterprise operations leader responsible for modernizing and scaling the operating foundation that powers ENGAGE (Training Operations) globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will establish and lead a Global Center of Excellence (CoE), driving AI-enabled operational transformation across Learning &amp;amp; Enablement (L&amp;amp;E) through scalable workflows, governance, automation, analytics, and operational discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is focused on improving how global systems, teams, and processes work together enabling ENGAGE to operate with greater predictability, visibility, efficiency, and commercial alignment across regions and programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a transformation year for Learning &amp;amp; Enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As learner demand, partners, SKUs, and regional complexity continue to scale, traditional operating models are no longer sufficient. Success now requires scalable operating mechanisms, AI-enabled workflows, stronger governance, and clearer operational accountability across regions and programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will help ENGAGE scale sustainably by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving operational efficiency and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reducing manual dependency and operational friction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increasing visibility into demand, risk, and capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating operational improvements into measurable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will help shape how Learning &amp;amp; Enablement operates in an increasingly AI-enabled environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Operating Model &amp;amp; CoE Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and lead the Global Center of Excellence (CoE) for ENGAGE operations, governance, tooling, and analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and operationalize a scalable hub-and-spoke operating model balancing global consistency with strong regional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize planning cadences, operational playbooks, decision rights, and execution frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed accountability, operational rigor, and measurable outcomes into global reviews and operating rhythms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Enabled Operations &amp;amp; Workflow Transformation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the evolution of ENGAGE’s AI-enabled operational workflows, automation strategy, and operational telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize real-time KPIs, dashboards, and exception monitoring to improve visibility into demand, risk, and operational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive automation and intelligent workflow design across scheduling, forecasting, certification, onboarding, and partner operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish governance principles for AI-enabled workflows, ensuring reliability, transparency, scalability, and measurable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Operations &amp;amp; Revenue Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Revenue Operations, and Commercialization teams to improve forecasting rigor, operational controls, utilization visibility, and scalable revenue-supporting processes globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational improvements into measurable business outcomes, including capacity unlock, reduced partner spend, improved utilization, and operational efficiency gains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support executive-grade reporting, operational visibility, and scalable governance mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed operational controls aligned with long-term scalability and audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Governance &amp;amp; Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build globally consistent operational governance across planning, reporting, exception handling, workflow controls, and operational oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear ownership models, escalation paths, and decision rights to reduce ambiguity and execution friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure operational resilience, compliance readiness, and structured risk mitigation across regions and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Leadership &amp;amp; Global Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead global adoption of standardized workflows, governance frameworks, and AI-enabled operating practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive consistent operational maturity and execution standards across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic advisor to L&amp;amp;E and operational leadership on scalability, operational health, and organizational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence across distributed, matrixed teams to drive alignment, accountability, and operational consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A predictable, scalable global operating model with clear ownership and operational accountability, while also supporting regional nuances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improved visibility into global demand, capacity, operational health, and execution risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduced operational friction, cycle times, and manual intervention across core ENGAGE workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable business impact through improved efficiency, utilization, scalability, and operational consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increased adoption of standardized workflows, automation, and AI-enabled tooling across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A stronger governance and operational foundation supporting long-term L&amp;amp;E scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in GTM Operations, Revenue Operations, Enablement Operations, Program Leadership, or Operational Transformation within high-growth global technology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building and scaling enterprise operating models, governance frameworks, and cross-functional execution mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading AI-enabled operational transformation initiatives, including automation, analytics, workflow modernization, and scalable process design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and operational acumen, including forecasting, revenue operations, utilization economics, and business performance drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Finance, Legal, Strategy, Product, and Revenue leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical rigor, systems thinking, and executive-level communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience modernizing and scaling enablement operations through process, tooling, and operating model transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with analytics platforms, data workflows, or Databricks technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success implementing AI and automation solutions within operational workflows at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to audit processes, SOX readiness, or public-company operational and financial controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in globally distributed, cross-functional environments with complex stakeholder alignment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help shape the operating foundation that enables ENGAGE and Learning &amp;amp; Enablement to scale with greater speed, consistency, and operational discipline in an AI-enabled environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility role with broad cross-functional influence, focused on improving how systems, workflows, governance, and automation come together to support customer and business outcomes globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are energized by simplifying complexity, building scalable operating mechanisms, and driving meaningful operational transformation, this role offers the opportunity to create lasting impact across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Databricks is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. The pay range(s) for this role is listed below and represents the expected base salary range for non-commissionable roles or on-target earnings for commissionable roles.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, relevant certifications and training, and specific work location. Based on the factors above, Databricks anticipated utilizing the full width of the range. The total compensation package for this position may also include eligibility for annual performance bonus, equity, and the benefits listed above. For more information regarding which range your location is in visit our page &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/sites/default/files/2024-08/us-pay-zone-mapping.pdf&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$148,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$204,250 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$133,700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$183,800 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$126,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$173,600 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 4 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$118,900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,450 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the data and AI company. More than 10,000 organizations worldwide — including Comcast, Condé Nast, Grammarly, and over 50% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform to unify and democratize data, analytics and AI. Databricks is headquartered in San Francisco, with offices around the globe and was founded by the original creators of Lakehouse, Apache Spark™, Delta Lake and MLflow. To learn more, follow Databricks on&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 54, 33);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 54, 33);&quot; href=&quot;https://twitter.com/databricks&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://twitter.com/databricks&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1700237575733000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw03FL8fJvOD97ytN02f5G2C&quot;&gt;Twitter&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 54, 33);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1700237575733000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw15dLk3q8VxTfHEgCUg7NSt&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 54, 33);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/databricksinc&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.facebook.com/databricksinc&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1700237575733000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw39EcncitnlqV72EG2-RqXJ&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;SLSQ227R838&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Consulting &amp;amp; Systems Integrator (C&amp;amp;SI) organization accelerates Databricks&#39; growth by building and managing strategic relationships with the world&#39;s leading data and technology services companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;RSI Portfolio Leader&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead a high-performing team responsible for driving the strategic go-to-market motions across Databricks&#39; Managed Gold Portfolio of Systems Integrator (SI) partners. Serving as a player-coach, you will define and execute a cohesive portfolio strategy while enabling your team to grow and scale some of Databricks&#39; most strategic partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will focus on expanding executive mindshare, accelerating joint revenue growth, creating scalable partnership models, and driving innovation through deeper collaboration with SI partners. You will work cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Marketing, and Partner teams to maximize the impact of the partner ecosystem and deliver measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Vice President of System Integrator Partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of global alliance professionals responsible for managing Databricks&#39; Managed Gold Portfolio of Systems Integrator partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute portfolio strategies that drive growth, scale, and long-term value across strategic partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand and deepen partnerships through jointly developed business plans that deliver predictable, recurring revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage C-suite executives to shape global strategies, align investment priorities, and establish shared business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate Databricks and partner adoption by identifying new market opportunities, expanding use cases, and driving joint customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute partner enablement and training strategies that increase partner capabilities, grow practices, and expand technical and sales expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure strategic investments and establish repeatable programs around joint intellectual property, solutions, and go-to-market initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead joint go-to-market campaigns, executive events, and thought leadership activities that increase market awareness, drive customer adoption, and generate new business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain trusted executive relationships across all levels of partner organizations to strengthen strategic alignment and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage joint business plans with clear governance and measurable success metrics across Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Training, Product, and Partner organizations to ensure alignment and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience building, managing, and scaling strategic partnerships with global organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of successfully leading a portfolio of Regional and Global System Integrator (RSI/GSI) partnerships and delivering measurable business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of alliance organizations, including executive stakeholders, organizational structures, business strategies, partner cultures, market offerings, and joint value propositions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience launching, scaling, and driving business outcomes with Global System Integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain expertise in enterprise Data, Analytics, AI, and cloud technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive global partner management experience spanning the Americas (AMER), Europe, Middle East &amp;amp; Africa (EMEA), and Asia-Pacific (APAC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing strategic channel relationships and leading complex commercial negotiations and partnership agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success operating in high-growth, entrepreneurial organizations and helping scale businesses through periods of rapid expansion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive presence with the ability to influence C-level stakeholders and align cross-functional teams around shared business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic planning, operational execution, and people leadership skills with a demonstrated ability to build and lead high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
