&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CSQ327R104&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and lead a team of Delivery Solution Architects (DSAs) responsible for the post-sales success of Databricks&#39; largest Financial Services customers. This is one of the most consequential delivery leadership roles in the company. The customers in your portfolio anchor a strategic vertical for Databricks, and your team&#39;s work directly determines how quickly Data and AI transforms how they do business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a DSA Manager you set the technical strategy across your portfolio, decide where to invest your team&#39;s capacity, and partner with Sales, Pre-Sales, Professional Services, and our Systems Integrator ecosystem to move use cases from kickoff to production. You are a hands-on technical sponsor and trusted advisor to a select group of customers, including their C-suite. You build the systems, operating cadences, and playbooks that make your team and the broader DSA practice sharper over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The DSAs you lead are senior technical talent, drawn from principal-level solution architecture, top-tier consulting, or senior engineering backgrounds. Hiring, coaching, and growing this team is the heart of the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, and develop a high-performing DSA team. Own career growth, calibrated performance management, and individual development plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own capacity planning and investment forecasting across the FINS portfolio. Defend investment decisions with data, alongside sales and field leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Pre-Sales, Professional Services, and Systems Integrator partners to accelerate use case delivery and reduce customer risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive measurable customer outcomes: use-case throughput, time-to-production, consumption growth, and renewal rates. Forecast each across your portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a programmatic approach to running the business. Build the systems, operating cadences, and playbooks that scale the DSA practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and promote the value proposition of the DSA role with our internal partners and our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing a customer-facing technical team (DSA, Solution Architect, Technical Account Manager, Customer Success Engineer, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership of a team of pre-sales or post-sales technical talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of putting data and AI workloads into production at scale, e.g., as a delivery architect, project manager, DevOps engineer, or service or product owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversant with the business problems and Data and AI use cases in financial services (banking, capital markets, insurance, or asset management preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for building systems, not just running them. A bias for growing people, not just managing them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of overachievement against quota, Goals or similar objective targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or equivalent experience through work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can travel up to 30% when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
