&lt;p&gt;While candidates in the listed location(s) are encouraged for this role, candidates in other locations will be considered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is seeking a Senior Financial Analyst to join our Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team. In this role, you will report to the Senior Finance Manager / Director of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A and help empower the broader FP&amp;amp;A organization. You will play a key role in building and managing core strategic planning processes, as well as partnering with leaders across functions to support budgeting, forecasting, and ongoing financial management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support long and short-term planning processes, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of the planning calendar with clearly communicated timelines, deliverables, and expectations with all planning stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring system snapshots are completed accurately and on time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building driver-based financial models to optimize resource allocation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing executive-ready materials, including financial models, scenario analyses, and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support financial modeling for capital raising and coordinate across FP&amp;amp;A, Investor Relations, and Treasury&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of Executive and Board reporting materials, ensuring accuracy and clarity of financial insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ad hoc analyses and strategic projects to support senior leaders across Finance and Investor Relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and lead process and system optimization initiatives, including opportunities for automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we look for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Masters in Business Administration from a top tier program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in corporate finance, management consulting, or investment banking; experience in the software or SaaS industry is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Google Sheets or Excel, including the ability to build and maintain complex financial models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage best-in-class AI to upskill and architect sophisticated, model-driven solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize data to uncover outcome driven insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to grasp the strategic ‘big picture’.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and the ability to prioritize and manage multiple objectives in a fast-paced environment while meeting deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the three statement financial model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
